# No Application Restart Rule

## Rule: Do not restart the application during testing

**Prohibition:** Never run `go run main.go`, `docker-compose up`, or any other application startup commands during testing or debugging sessions.

**Reason:** The application is already running and available for testing.

**Allowed:** 
- Only test API endpoints using `curl`, `wget`, or similar tools
- Check application logs if needed
- Stop the application only when explicitly requested by the user

**Examples of what NOT to do:**
- `go run main.go`
- `docker-compose up -d`
- `docker-compose restart`
- Any command that starts or restarts the application

**Examples of what TO do:**
- `curl http://localhost:9966/api/v1/health`
- `curl -X POST http://localhost:9966/api/v1/users/login`
- Check logs: `docker-compose logs app`
- Test endpoints without restarting

**Exception:** Only restart the application when the user explicitly requests it or when there are code changes that require a restart.# No Application Restart Rule

